WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.050
Next you read the island list and
the reconciliation side by side.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.463
Each row now carries its
disposition from Chapter 3.

3
00:00:07.463 --> 00:00:11.188
Two rows aren't ready for
hand-off, so the flag stays false.

4
00:00:11.188 --> 00:00:15.291
The web front end carries the
authorizing official's acceptance,

5
00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:17.951
so it becomes ready once
it has an S P N owner.

6
00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:22.338
That's the point: which is the point:
an incomplete list never goes.

7
00:00:22.338 --> 00:00:23.662
Then the write path.

8
00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:27.876
A dry run with the approved hash
reports the four writes it would send.

9
00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:31.940
Applying it to the fake sends them,
and the results tell the operator

10
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.787
what comes next, such as installing
each new account on its hosts.

11
00:00:35.787 --> 00:00:40.051
Finally you pass a hash nobody
approved, and it refuses outright.

12
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:43.510
The full suite is five hundred
thirteen passing tests.
